# Citation File Format — see https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# When you use vibe-qc in published work, please cite it via this file.
# GitHub and recent GitLab versions render a "Cite this repository" sidebar.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use vibe-qc in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "vibe-qc: a quantum-chemistry code for molecules and solids"
abstract: >
  vibe-qc is an open-source electronic-structure code with a Python
  frontend over a C++17 core. It implements restricted/unrestricted
  Hartree-Fock and Kohn-Sham DFT for molecules and 1D/2D/3D periodic
  systems, MP2, D3(BJ) dispersion, and analytic atomic gradients.
  Backed by libint (Gaussian integrals), libxc (XC functionals), and
  spglib (crystal symmetry). The long-term target is the Cyclic
  Cluster Model at correlated levels of theory (MP2 → CCSD(T)) for
  defect chemistry on solid-state systems.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Peintinger
    given-names: Michael F.
    website: "https://vibe-qc.com/"
version: 0.17.2
date-released: "2026-09-13"
url: "https://vibe-qc.com/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vibe-qc/vibe-qc"
license: MPL-2.0
keywords:
  - quantum chemistry
  - electronic structure
  - density functional theory
  - Hartree-Fock
  - Møller-Plesset
  - periodic boundary conditions
  - cyclic cluster model
  - solid-state chemistry
  - Gaussian basis sets
  - open source

# When users employ specific components of vibe-qc, the references
# below should be cited alongside the software itself. The
# documentation page docs/citing.md walks through which to pick.
